WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.227 --> 00:00:04.394
- We put our foot down and
insisted in being respected

00:00:05.449 --> 00:00:06.639
even though we're prisoners.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.458
She said who are you to ask for my name?

00:00:08.458 --> 00:00:09.417
What's your name?

00:00:09.417 --> 00:00:12.000
You have a limited time to stay

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:14.080
on Earth.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.636
We do not care whether
the cat is black or white

00:00:18.636 --> 00:00:20.654
as long as it can catch mice.

00:00:20.654 --> 00:00:24.821
But humility is one of the
most important qualities

00:00:26.606 --> 00:00:28.147
which you must have.

00:00:28.147 --> 00:00:31.391
I was paralyzed because it made my day.

00:00:31.391 --> 00:00:35.210
Our attitudes towards
any country is determined

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.943
by the attitude of that
country to our struggle.

00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:42.846
But our brain said if you
don't talk with this man

00:00:42.846 --> 00:00:44.896
your country will go up in flames.

00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:48.079
It is the desire of every freedom fighter

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:51.078
to disappear under a cloud of glory.

00:00:51.078 --> 00:00:52.832
I don't know if I have paralyzed you.

00:00:52.832 --> 00:00:53.665
- [Ted] No, no, no, no, no, I.

00:00:53.665 --> 00:00:55.271
(audience cheering loudly)

00:00:55.271 --> 00:00:58.349
- He was a South African
anti-apartheid revolutionary,

00:00:58.349 --> 00:01:00.438
politician, and philanthropist.

00:01:00.438 --> 00:01:04.964
He served as President of
South Africa from 1994 to 1999.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.842
In South Africa, he's often described

00:01:06.842 --> 00:01:08.624
as the Father of the Nation.

00:01:08.624 --> 00:01:10.231
He's Nelson Mandela and here are his

00:01:10.231 --> 00:01:12.109
top 10 rules for success.

00:01:12.109 --> 00:01:15.100
(quick sibilant music)

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.762
- How did you get the racist guards

00:01:16.762 --> 00:01:18.404
to treat you with respect?

00:01:18.404 --> 00:01:20.819
You were in prison and you
said I will only respond

00:01:20.819 --> 00:01:23.518
to the name Mandela or Mr. Mandela.

00:01:23.518 --> 00:01:26.513
- You must fight the battle for dignity.

00:01:26.513 --> 00:01:27.346
- Um hmm.

00:01:27.346 --> 00:01:29.157
- On the very first day you go to jail.

00:01:29.157 --> 00:01:30.231
- [Oprah] Really?

00:01:30.231 --> 00:01:32.314
- And that's what we did.

00:01:33.288 --> 00:01:37.455
We put our foot down and
insisted in being respected

00:01:38.312 --> 00:01:40.169
even though we're prisoners.

00:01:40.169 --> 00:01:42.468
And we, thankfully, succeeded in that.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.468
When I found

00:01:45.292 --> 00:01:47.292
some place in my country

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.043
and a lady inside the telephone

00:01:52.697 --> 00:01:55.697
I then asked, to whom am I speaking?

00:01:58.146 --> 00:02:00.144
She said, you're speaking to me.

00:02:00.144 --> 00:02:02.759
(audience laughing)

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:06.102
I said, well, lady, I
know I am speaking to you

00:02:06.102 --> 00:02:08.655
but what's your name?

00:02:08.655 --> 00:02:10.398
She said, who are you to ask for my name?

00:02:10.398 --> 00:02:11.430
What's your name?

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.459
(audience laughing loudly)

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:18.114
I said, well, lady, as soon
as you tell me your name,

00:02:18.114 --> 00:02:19.697
I'll tell you mine.

00:02:20.603 --> 00:02:24.770
But as we argued as to who
should tell his or her name,

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.663
she became very cross.

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:32.777
And she said, you seem
to be a backward person.

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:35.602
Have you passed your matric?

00:02:35.602 --> 00:02:39.070
Now, a matric our country is a university

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.653
and re-examination.

00:02:41.831 --> 00:02:45.609
And I said, well, lady,
you must be very careful

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:48.651
because if the qualification
to speak to you is

00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:51.819
the possession of a matric certificate

00:02:51.819 --> 00:02:56.201
I might work hard and
pass my matric and be in

00:02:56.201 --> 00:02:58.368
the same class as you are.

00:02:59.639 --> 00:03:01.056
That was treason.

00:03:02.713 --> 00:03:03.546
She said,

00:03:05.193 --> 00:03:07.710
you will never be in my class

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:08.985
and banged the telephone.

00:03:08.985 --> 00:03:11.870
(audience laughing)

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.054
How I wish she were here today.

00:03:15.054 --> 00:03:19.221
(audience cheering and applauding loudly)

00:03:31.502 --> 00:03:35.502
She would now discover
that I have achieved more

00:03:36.468 --> 00:03:38.135
than pass my matric.

00:03:38.135 --> 00:03:42.302
I hated oppression and when
I think about the past,

00:03:43.197 --> 00:03:45.650
the type of things they did,

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.733
I feel angry.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.803
You have a limited time to stay

00:03:52.107 --> 00:03:52.940
on Earth.

00:03:54.052 --> 00:03:58.052
You must try and use that
period for the pebbles

00:03:59.366 --> 00:04:03.533
of transforming your country
into what you desire it to be.

00:04:04.531 --> 00:04:08.855
- What can assure me, as a
human being, and a concerned

00:04:08.855 --> 00:04:13.797
African American, that the
ANC will indeed have a fiscal,

00:04:13.797 --> 00:04:18.475
solvent policy that will
continue the use of the resources

00:04:18.475 --> 00:04:20.517
of South Africa in a meaningful way?

00:04:20.517 --> 00:04:22.366
Or should I put it more succinctly?

00:04:22.366 --> 00:04:25.527
Will your economy be based
on the Marxist system,

00:04:25.527 --> 00:04:28.360
socialism, or capitalism, or both?

00:04:29.777 --> 00:04:32.679
- I knew that was the
question you wanted to ask.

00:04:32.679 --> 00:04:36.846
(audience laughing and applauding loudly)

00:04:40.957 --> 00:04:44.438
I am happy that you have had
the courage to put it directly.

00:04:44.438 --> 00:04:48.021
(audience laughing loudly)

00:04:49.807 --> 00:04:52.640
We are not concerned with martyrs.

00:04:54.407 --> 00:04:57.157
We are not concerned with labels.

00:04:58.183 --> 00:05:01.488
We are practical men and women

00:05:01.488 --> 00:05:04.526
whose solutions are dictated
by the actual conditions

00:05:04.526 --> 00:05:06.526
existing in our country.

00:05:07.737 --> 00:05:11.904
As somebody has said, we
do not care whether the cat

00:05:13.202 --> 00:05:17.601
is black or white as long
as it can catch mice.

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:21.434
The first thing is to
be honest with yourself.

00:05:23.753 --> 00:05:27.003
You can never have an impact on society

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:34.214
if you have not changed yourself.

00:05:35.428 --> 00:05:38.816
And one of the most important weapons

00:05:38.816 --> 00:05:42.816
in changing yourself is
to recognize that peace,

00:05:44.363 --> 00:05:49.068
I mean people everywhere
in the world want peace.

00:05:49.068 --> 00:05:53.235
But humility is one of the
most important qualities

00:05:55.138 --> 00:05:58.971
which you must have
because if you are humble,

00:06:02.182 --> 00:06:04.765
if you make people realize that

00:06:06.684 --> 00:06:09.198
you are no threat for them

00:06:09.198 --> 00:06:11.615
then people will embrace you.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.233
They will listen to you.

00:06:14.233 --> 00:06:17.474
- Was Muhammad Ali a hero of yours?

00:06:17.474 --> 00:06:19.257
- Well, naturally.

00:06:19.257 --> 00:06:23.634
As far as boxing is concerned
and what he has done,

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:25.366
he was my hero.

00:06:25.366 --> 00:06:28.533
Just like Ruben here, this is my hero.

00:06:29.498 --> 00:06:32.785
- What did you say to him
when he told you he loved you?

00:06:32.785 --> 00:06:36.452
Well I was paralyzed
because it made my day.

00:06:37.383 --> 00:06:40.550
(audience applauding)

00:06:44.328 --> 00:06:48.495
- So what leaders of the
20th Century do you admire?

00:06:50.339 --> 00:06:52.887
- Well, I've answered that question.

00:06:52.887 --> 00:06:55.715
It's the not question of a leader,

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:58.458
it's a question of a human being.

00:06:58.458 --> 00:07:02.625
Who does something to make an
ordinary individual to feel

00:07:04.131 --> 00:07:07.298
I am a human being and I have a future

00:07:10.188 --> 00:07:14.355
and I can go to bed feeling
strong and full of hope.

00:07:16.585 --> 00:07:19.305
- And you have praised
Fidel Castro as a leader

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:24.128
of human rights and said that
Cuba was one of the countries

00:07:24.128 --> 00:07:26.389
that's head and shoulders
above all other countries

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:28.649
in human rights despite
the fact that documents

00:07:28.649 --> 00:07:31.194
at the United Nations and
elsewhere show that Cuba

00:07:31.194 --> 00:07:32.368
is one of the worst.

00:07:32.368 --> 00:07:36.081
I was just wondering, are
these your models of leaders

00:07:36.081 --> 00:07:39.510
of human rights and if so,
would you want a Gaddafi

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:42.263
or an Arafat or a Castro to be a future

00:07:42.263 --> 00:07:44.430
President of South Africa?

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.900
- One of the mistakes

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:52.497
which has some political analysts make

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.370
is to think that their enemies

00:07:57.913 --> 00:07:59.543
should be our enemies.

00:07:59.543 --> 00:08:03.710
(audience cheering and applauding loudly)

00:08:21.823 --> 00:08:22.656
That

00:08:24.801 --> 00:08:25.634
we can

00:08:26.751 --> 00:08:28.501
and we will never do.

00:08:30.505 --> 00:08:34.588
We have our own struggle
which we are conducting.

00:08:36.205 --> 00:08:40.372
We are grateful to the world
for supporting our struggle.

00:08:43.086 --> 00:08:47.789
But, nevertheless, we are
an independent organization

00:08:47.789 --> 00:08:49.456
with its own policy.

00:08:50.811 --> 00:08:54.978
And the attitude of every
country towards our attitude

00:08:56.455 --> 00:09:00.309
towards any country is
determined by the attitude

00:09:00.309 --> 00:09:02.242
of that country to our struggle.

00:09:02.242 --> 00:09:06.409
(audience cheering and applauding loudly)

00:09:17.243 --> 00:09:18.410
Yassir Arafat,

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:23.194
Colonel Gaddafi,

00:09:25.971 --> 00:09:27.054
Fidel Castro,

00:09:28.908 --> 00:09:31.968
support our struggle to the hilt.

00:09:31.968 --> 00:09:36.135
(audience cheering and applauding loudly)

00:09:39.547 --> 00:09:43.547
There is no reason
whatsoever why we should have

00:09:44.562 --> 00:09:48.312
any hesitation about
hailing their commitment

00:09:51.084 --> 00:09:55.251
to human rights as they are
being demanded in South Africa.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:10:00.442
Our attitude is based
solely on the fact that they

00:10:00.442 --> 00:10:03.942
fully support the anti-apartheid struggle.

00:10:04.936 --> 00:10:09.098
They do not support it only in rhetoric,

00:10:09.098 --> 00:10:13.517
they are placing resources
at our disposal for us

00:10:13.517 --> 00:10:16.345
(audience applauding loudly)

00:10:16.345 --> 00:10:18.095
to win this struggle.

00:10:22.832 --> 00:10:24.265
That is the position.

00:10:24.265 --> 00:10:26.640
- You'd also said to me
one evening, you said,

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.977
we made the brain dominate the blood.

00:10:29.977 --> 00:10:34.144
- Our emotions said the
white minority is an enemy,

00:10:36.371 --> 00:10:39.347
we must never talk to them.

00:10:39.347 --> 00:10:43.430
But our brain said if you
don't talk to this man,

00:10:44.286 --> 00:10:47.257
your country will go up in flames.

00:10:47.257 --> 00:10:48.090
And,

00:10:49.312 --> 00:10:51.786
for many years to come,

00:10:51.786 --> 00:10:55.079
this country would be
engulfed in rivers of blood.

00:10:55.079 --> 00:10:59.246
So we had to reconcile that
conflict and our talking

00:11:02.447 --> 00:11:06.197
to the enemy was the
result of the domination

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:10.110
of the brain over emotions.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:13.527
- And then you were convicted in 1964 for

00:11:16.337 --> 00:11:19.639
conspiracy against the state and in your,

00:11:19.639 --> 00:11:23.661
when you pleaded you said
that I am willing to die

00:11:23.661 --> 00:11:25.674
for this cause.

00:11:25.674 --> 00:11:28.300
This is a very tough thing to say.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:29.133
- Yes,

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:32.334
I had to say that,

00:11:32.334 --> 00:11:36.501
not from a spirit of bravado
but because I genuinely felt

00:11:37.395 --> 00:11:40.032
that they were going to hang us.

00:11:40.032 --> 00:11:44.322
And it is the desire of
every freedom fighter

00:11:44.322 --> 00:11:47.239
to disappear under a cloud of glory

00:11:48.171 --> 00:11:51.118
rather than that of shame.

00:11:51.118 --> 00:11:54.218
It is the task of a freedom fighter

00:11:54.218 --> 00:11:58.622
when you see that the
end of your days has come

00:11:58.622 --> 00:12:02.455
to leave a tradition of
bravery, determination

00:12:04.097 --> 00:12:07.347
to face even death for your principles.

00:12:08.428 --> 00:12:10.428
And, I thought about it.

00:12:11.803 --> 00:12:14.447
It was not because I was brave

00:12:14.447 --> 00:12:17.732
but because one had a duty to perform

00:12:17.732 --> 00:12:19.767
at that moment.

00:12:19.767 --> 00:12:21.767
I have dedicated my life

00:12:24.777 --> 00:12:26.110
to this struggle

00:12:28.034 --> 00:12:29.867
of the African people.

00:12:32.583 --> 00:12:33.666
I have fought

00:12:36.082 --> 00:12:38.082
against white domination

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.397
and I have fought

00:12:44.117 --> 00:12:46.200
against black domination.

00:12:47.819 --> 00:12:49.152
I have cherished

00:12:50.848 --> 00:12:51.681
the idea

00:12:53.364 --> 00:12:56.031
of a democratic and free society

00:12:58.002 --> 00:13:00.352
in which all persons

00:13:00.352 --> 00:13:02.459
will live together

00:13:02.459 --> 00:13:05.792
in harmony and with equal opportunities.

00:13:14.073 --> 00:13:15.156
It is an idea

00:13:17.556 --> 00:13:18.889
for which I hope

00:13:20.384 --> 00:13:21.301
to live for

00:13:22.909 --> 00:13:24.576
and to see realized.

00:13:28.107 --> 00:13:29.107
But my Lord,

00:13:31.001 --> 00:13:32.251
if it needs be.

00:13:34.594 --> 00:13:35.677
It is an idea

00:13:37.203 --> 00:13:39.786
for which I am prepared to die.

00:13:41.321 --> 00:13:42.238
For anybody

00:13:43.787 --> 00:13:46.037
who changes his principles,

00:13:47.036 --> 00:13:49.543
depending on whom he is dealing,

00:13:49.543 --> 00:13:52.340
that is not a man who can lead a nation.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:56.507
(audience applauding and cheering loudly)

00:14:20.163 --> 00:14:21.080
Apparently,

00:14:22.884 --> 00:14:23.801
Mr. Koppel,

00:14:25.323 --> 00:14:27.603
you have not listened to my argument.

00:14:27.603 --> 00:14:29.270
If you have done so,

00:14:30.592 --> 00:14:34.509
then you have not been
serious in examining it.

00:14:35.413 --> 00:14:38.830
I have replied to one of our friends here

00:14:40.145 --> 00:14:44.312
that I have refused to be
drawn into the differences

00:14:45.653 --> 00:14:49.820
that exist between various
communities inside the USA.

00:14:50.963 --> 00:14:55.130
You have not commented that
I am going to offend anybody

00:14:56.081 --> 00:15:00.363
by refusing to involve myself
in the internal affairs

00:15:00.363 --> 00:15:02.895
of the USA, of the USA.

00:15:02.895 --> 00:15:06.645
(audience applauding loudly)

00:15:08.508 --> 00:15:13.131
Why are you so keen that
I should involve myself

00:15:13.131 --> 00:15:15.482
in the internal affairs of Cuba and Libya?

00:15:15.482 --> 00:15:16.315
- No.

00:15:16.315 --> 00:15:18.982
- I expect you to be consistent.

00:15:25.482 --> 00:15:27.130
I don't know if I have paralyzed you.

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.222
- No, no, no, no, I.

00:15:28.222 --> 00:15:32.389
(audience cheering and applauding loudly)

00:15:52.516 --> 00:15:53.349
No, I.

00:16:02.613 --> 00:16:03.446
I'm,

00:16:07.242 --> 00:16:10.358
I'm afraid, Mr. Mandela, that
paralysis does not set in

00:16:10.358 --> 00:16:12.775
quite that easily in my case.

00:16:13.839 --> 00:16:14.763
The point.

00:16:14.763 --> 00:16:18.513
(audience applauding loudly)

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:21.521
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:21.521 --> 00:16:24.608
I made this video because
Michael B. asked me to.

00:16:24.608 --> 00:16:26.505
So, if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:16:26.505 --> 00:16:28.680
to profile next, leave
it in the comments below

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:29.900
and I'll see what I can do.

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.737
I would also love to know
which of Nelson Mandela's

00:16:31.737 --> 00:16:34.600
top 10 rules had the
biggest impact on you,

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.728
is going to change your life in some way.

00:16:36.728 --> 00:16:38.705
Leave it in the comments and
I'll join the discussion.

00:16:38.705 --> 00:16:41.009
And one last thing, my goal
with this channel is to get

00:16:41.009 --> 00:16:43.833
to one million subscribers
so anything that you can do

00:16:43.833 --> 00:16:46.368
to think of to share the
video, tell friends about it,

00:16:46.368 --> 00:16:49.514
add it to the playlist, Tweet
about it, let people know,

00:16:49.514 --> 00:16:51.269
I'd really, really, really appreciate it.

00:16:51.269 --> 00:16:52.932
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:52.932 --> 00:16:56.070
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.655
(quick sibilant music)

